   "status": "FIXED in round 2: Container._scan_stream() stores the exact end of the last validated block in valid_end and the examined byte count in scanned_end; modified() compares against scanned_end. The rows above now show valid_end_minus_file_size == 0 and modified_state_on_reopen == 'same'. Regression tests: nanomem_standalone/tests/test_reopen_and_concurrency.py.",
   "line": "3.0.0 container.py:603",
   "code": "self.valid_end = pos   # pos = align_up(end) after the last block",
   "explanation": "Container.scan() rounds valid_end UP to the 64-byte alignment boundary, but append_block() (line 643) sets valid_end = start + len(blob), the exact end. A file written by one instance and re-opened by another therefore has valid_end > st_size, so Container.modified() takes the 'st_size < valid_end' branch and returns 'replaced' forever. VaultEngine._reload_if_modified() then calls _full_reload() on EVERY search/get/stats: it re-derives the scrypt key, re-reads the whole file, re-verifies every block HMAC and rebuilds the arena.",
   "frequency_measured": "30 of 31 vaults of assorted sizes reported 'replaced' on reopen (only a last block that happens to end 64-byte aligned escapes)",
   "fix": "valid_end must be the true end of the last validated block (pos before align_up, or min(align_up(end), st_size)); align_up belongs on the NEXT read/write offset only."
